{"ts":"2026-07-25T07:10:29.303Z","author":"unknown","author_source":"unknown","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-38bskj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Public SDK surface shape: 881 exports behind one flat entrypoint with no capability tiering and a 250ms eager import cost"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Importing the published SDK entry yields 881 runtime exports from a single module (693 functions plus 188 values/classes), and package.json declares only four subpaths: '.', './sdk', './sdk/runtime', './sdk/testing'. Everything else — query, governance, graph, merge, test, extension, cli-contracts — is flattened into that one namespace, so a package author who needs one primitive loads the whole graph: 'import(dist/cli-bundle/sdk.js)' costs 289ms against a 41ms bare-node baseline, the same as importing the entire CLI (286ms). The namespace is also undifferentiated: stable authoring primitives sit beside per-command flag-contract constants (ACTIVITY_COMMANDER_STRING_OPTION_CONTRACTS, CALENDAR_FLAG_CONTRACTS, ...) with nothing marking which symbols are the supported authoring surface. src/sdk/index.ts is 35 'export *' lines, which is why the surface grows silently. Duplicate check: searched SDK surface/entrypoint/subpath/tiering/import-cost all-status. pm-e6tm5c owns the snapshot and breaking-change gate — it will freeze whatever shape exists, so shaping must precede or accompany it; pm-9x6e (closed) zeroed the private-core import baseline in the other direction; pm-ds3b (closed) documented the promoted primitives; pm-agou is the GA stability ADR; pm-feecbs governs external package conformance, not host export shape. None of them own how the surface is partitioned or what it costs to import."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["api","architecture","area:sdk","ecosystem","packages","performance"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-25T07:10:29.303Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T07:10:29.303Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"unknown"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":1200},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The public SDK is partitioned into documented subpath entrypoints that mirror the internal module families (at minimum core item/query, governance, graph, merge, extension authoring, testing, and cli-contracts), each independently importable; a package author can import one family without loading the others, proven by a measured import-cost table in the repo showing per-entry cost against the bare-node baseline; the flat './sdk' entry keeps working unchanged as an aggregate so no existing consumer breaks; every export is classified as supported authoring surface, contract data, or advanced/internal-but-exported, and that classification is the input pm-e6tm5c snapshots; docs/SDK.md and the extension author docs route by entrypoint; no export is removed and no external package requires changes to keep working"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Make building a pm package cheap to start and cheap to run: a small, tiered, independently loadable public API"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"The SDK is the product surface for the whole ecosystem; an 881-symbol flat namespace that costs a quarter second to import is both a discovery barrier for authors and a fixed latency cost in every extension process"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"pm-e6tm5c is about to turn the current shape into a frozen compatibility contract, and pm-9rgaal declares SDK-complete core as an outcome milestone — shaping after the freeze is a breaking change"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-usfg"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"6b89b3377abbe3e67ea8ba506f80f21f85bdaf033020c0318964a1fba2308a49","message":"Filed from the ecosystem review: measured export count and import cost, deduped against the SDK promotion lineage"}
